        <title type="html"><![CDATA[In Firefox, & inside at-scope blocks has no implicit specificity]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27723</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27723"/>
        <updated>2025-09-01T08:52:33.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43580235?u=cae42d5a371dd041072ce6d85a1808de05535be8&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">CSS WG have decided that <code class="notranslate">&amp;</code> inside <code class="notranslate">@scope</code> blocks should be treated like <code class="notranslate">:where(:scope)</code>. This has specificity implications, see the updated docs: <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@scope#specificity_in_scope" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@scope#specificity_in_scope</a></p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>Spec:</strong> <a href="https://redirect.github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9740">https://redirect.github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9740</a> (WIP)</li>
<li><strong>Bugzilla:</strong> <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1975531" rel="nofollow">1975531</a></li>
<li><strong>WPT:</strong> <a href="https://redirect.github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/53831">https://redirect.github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/53831</a> (WIP)</li>
</ul>
